    ],
    "summary" : "The coding discipline: build, run, test and save a project through the editor's own commands, and read and edit its live code surface. An application joins this discipline by realizing one of the chord Skills — which is what gives its place the coding focus — or by declaring a `codeSurface` for the reads and the one write. read_buffer and read_selection bind to the code-surface adapter, the same shape the writing Ability's own reads take for a prose document — a Skill that returns a value needs a compiled provider, never a recipe. replace_selection binds to the same adapter for the one reason a write needs a compiled provider too: an atomic disk write, Xcode's own proven chain, has no managed-UI recipe equivalent — it changes the file on disk, never types a keystroke, and refuses rather than overwrite a buffer with unsaved changes.",
    "tint" : "#B392F0",
